Leisaac teloperation feature is used to control the virtual arm in IsaacSim. This is used to generate high quality demonstration data through teloperation.
This video shows how to starts IsaacSIm and how to operate the virtual robotic arm. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y5pISY36cg4
This is the command to control robotic arm using keyboard for easier testing: ./isaaclab.sh -p scripts/environments/teleoperation/teleop_se3_agent.py --task Isaac-Lift-Cube-Franka-IK-Rel-v0 --num_envs 1 --teleop_device keyboard
LeRobotDatasheet: https://huggingface.co/blog/lerobot-datasets-v3
To install datasheet environment: pip install "https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/archive/33cad37054c2b594ceba57463e8f11ee374fa93c.zip"  # this will affect your local lerobot installation!
Hugging Face: https://huggingface.co/docs/lerobot/en/lerobot-dataset-v3
There are three pillars of data: 
Tabular data- low dimensional, high frequency signals (states, actions, timestamps)
Visual data- frames from the same episode/test are grouped, and videos are shared per camera
metadata- records describing feature names. dtypes, shapes, frame rates, normalization stats, and episode segmentation

